<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to reveal 1996 exports Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Brazil to reveal 1996 exports Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Ministry of Industry and Commerce will reveal exports for December and total exports for 1996 at 1430 local time/1630 GMT Tuesday, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Exports in the first three weeks of December totalled $2.843 billion with a daily average of $189.5 million.</p>
<p>In November, when Brazil posted a $853 million deficit, exports were $3.912 billion.</p>
<p>The markets speculate December may have seen another trade gap, of up to $1.5 billion.  December's trade balance, and the balance for 1996, are expected to be announced around mid-month.</p>
<p>((--Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
